  "raw": ", plug-in hybrid XC40 is the most stylish city car out there right now. And all Volvo wants to do is get it across America to you so you can take a test drive on the open road, or drive the thing in the office parking garage.\nThe XC40 is a great-looking vehicle from a design perspective, and it handles pretty well for a car that’s meant to pack a punch on the gas tank. In terms of its electric motor performance, that’s a whole other story. The vehicle’s electric motor doesn’t even turn when the driver is in neutral.\nVolvo did its usual thing on top of the XC40, putting a giant logo right on the center console, and adding a couple of words about hybrid and plug in batteries. But no mention about where the electric motor actually comes from—the Volvo “battery” is a standard, non-electric battery that doesn’t",
